  "description": "The comparator never calls a declared loss identical (x-compare). Recording b holds the same output payload as the uninterrupted recording a, byte for byte, and a gap marker besides: it says 5 bytes were lost, which a has no record of. Leaving the gap markers out would call the two identical and hide the declaration — a spurious marker, or payload a core filled in over a loss it had declared. So output is identical only when the gap markers are the same, line for line, as well as the payload; the end markers are left out, and input is compared as before.",
